Under-the-hood reality

A Unity Mesh is just structured data in memory:

Mesh
 ├─ Vector3[] vertices   ← positions (THIS is what you push)
 ├─ int[] triangles      ← index order
 ├─ Vector3[] normals    ← lighting directions
 ├─ Vector2[] uvs        ← texture mapping


When you “push” a vertex, you are doing this:
